{"id":"396775375","kind":"article","title":"单独的间隔重复记忆卡片是一种糟糕的交流媒介","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":["https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z1YhDPWyvzzkC79LFcF4DSTanKpEGpic8bAe","https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zHV9RymMTYzjYv8ioA3xaAs"],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"间隔重复 & 注意力管理","date":"2021-08-05","updated":"2022-08-06","votes":13,"comment_count":4,"minutes":1,"chars":518,"keywords":["间隔重复","记忆卡片","助记媒介","概念结构","叙事"],"summary":"文章指出，传统间隔重复卡片虽原子化、可按任意顺序呈现，却不容易传达高度结构化、依赖上下文的概念；把内容与整体及情感联系割裂，也会令他人的卡片难以学习。作者将助记媒介视为给卡片补上结构的一种思路。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/396775375","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"链接至本文（已汉化）"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"声明"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"MPzn7AHt\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4w269svvGhA2H5XFr6geaBbPTrxtJRpjt5TE\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">传统的间隔重复记忆卡片是原子化的</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>。每张卡片必须独立存在，可以在任何时候以任何顺序呈现。但是，这使得我们很难利用这些卡片来有效地传达一个本身就高度结构化且有序的概念。在实践中，概念通常依赖于其他概念，而情感显著性需要将这些概念与一个更大的整体联系起来（与<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z5gCpoFJJThDFHK1a7Vv3ssxF3kkjeRaTrJHK\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">深刻的理解需要强烈的个人联系（也是其结果）</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>矛盾）。叙事在这些方面表现出色（<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zvHfreBts9DHWRtztZihrGKuPsP5j8LSPLQn\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">文本的叙述作为认知脚手架</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>）。</p><p data-pid=\"084ZfPq4\">一个重要的影响：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z38fLX4H8oq9eXKnZH7wk8qDXfBLg2bxVyA2M\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">学习别人的间隔重复记忆卡片通常是无效的</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup>。</p><p data-pid=\"2EkMm0xQ\">这一观察是开发<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4rRX3qwSSJRsEkdXKwH2shamgHNeRthrMLiF\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">助记媒介</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup>的主要动机之一：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z5YjgWTaYfhWLrEbysgmDfFRcZ1yxgLeBeZac\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">助记媒介给原子化的间隔重复记忆卡片以结构</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup></p><h2 id=\"sec-1\">链接至本文（已汉化）</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"18gA8G0N\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"397037269\" href=\"#/post/397037269\">传统的间隔重复记忆卡片是原子化的</a></li><li data-pid=\"IVgXwc1J\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"397646854\" href=\"#/post/397646854\">助记媒介赋予通常原子化的间隔重复记忆卡片以结构</a></li><li data-pid=\"tzEEK_yV\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"397271029\" href=\"#/post/397271029\">学习别人的间隔重复记忆卡片通常是无效的</a></li><li data-pid=\"7LfHdSSC\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"408715726\" href=\"#/post/408715726\">我的间隔重复系统方法的不同之处</a></li><li data-pid=\"EUwIhHLy\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"550695797\" href=\"#/post/550695797\">先学再记</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-2\">声明</h2><p data-pid=\"2II_mNAk\">此内容发布由 Andy Matuschak 许可。未经允许，不得转载或修改。保留所有权利。</p><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"UbGnaaHv\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"http://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z1YhDPWyvzzkC79LFcF4DSTanKpEGpic8bAe\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Spaced repetition memory prompts alone are a poor communications medium</a></blockquote><p></p><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 传统的间隔重复记忆卡片是原子化的 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"397037269\" href=\"#/post/397037269\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 深刻的理解需要强烈的个人联系（也是其结果） <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"397575334\" href=\"#/post/397575334\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 文本的叙述作为认知脚手架 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"458799119\" href=\"#/post/458799119\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 学习另一个人的间隔重复记忆卡片通常是无效的 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"397271029\" href=\"#/post/397271029\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-5\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-5\">↩</a> 助记媒介 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"459483765\" href=\"#/post/459483765\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-6\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-6\">↩</a> 助记媒介赋予通常原子化的间隔重复记忆卡片以结构 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"397646854\" href=\"#/post/397646854\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"382699591","title":"在课堂上使用间隔重复软件的这七年","author":"tanagrabeast","votes":35,"minutes":166,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 间隔重复 & 注意力管理"},{"id":"397037269","title":"传统的间隔重复记忆卡片是原子化的","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":12,"minutes":1,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 间隔重复 & 注意力管理"},{"id":"550695797","title":"先学再记","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":18,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"459483765","title":"助记媒介（Mnemonic medium）","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":37,"minutes":6,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"397271029","title":"学习别人的间隔重复记忆卡片通常是无效的","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":22,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[],"rec_answers":[{"id":"2193593015","title":"从Anki过渡到Supermemo需要注意些什么呢？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":110,"minutes":4,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 110 赞同","evidence":"正文链接锚文本明确指向该译文标题或具体关键词。"}]}